# Cross-League Performance Translation Model (CLPTM) — Implementation Plan

## Background

The project already has exploratory scripts and raw data for Premier League and Bundesliga (23/24 and 24/25). The work is currently flat — all scripts and CSVs live in the root directory, multiple overlapping scripts exist ([Percentiling.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/Percentiling.py), [Percentiling2.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/Percentiling2.py), [addpercentiles.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/addpercentiles.py)), and the only "model" is a basic RandomForest on percentile columns.

This plan restructures everything into a **production-grade, config-driven, modular ML system** that a professional club could use.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Two data sources are currently in use:**
> 1. **FBRef [players_data-2024_2025.csv](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/players_data-2024_2025.csv)** — rich stats (xG, xA, progressive carries, etc.), covers 24/25 season only.
> 2. **Sofascore CSVs** in `Bundesliga_PlayerStats/` and `Prem_PlayerStats/` — goals/90, xG/90, tackles, etc., covers 23/24.
>
> For the transfer model to work (train on Season N, predict Season N+1), both sources must align or we use FBRef alone.
> **Recommendation:** Use FBRef as the primary source (richer features) and archive the Sofascore CSVs. Please confirm this direction.

> [!WARNING]
> **[transfertable.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/transfertable.py) has a syntax error** (indented block missing under `if col.endswith("_percentile"):`). This script is non-functional. It will be fixed and folded into the new pipeline.

> [!NOTE]
> **League Strength Coefficient** will be computed from UEFA coefficients / FBRef xG averages. We will start with a static config value that can be updated each season.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 0 — Cleanup & Restructure

All old scripts will be **moved** (not deleted) to `src/legacy/`. All raw CSVs go to `data/raw/`.

**New directory structure:**
```
TransferPred/
├── config/
│   └── config.yaml          # All paths, league params, thresholds
├── data/
│   ├── raw/                 # Original CSVs (untouched)
│   ├── interim/             # Mid-pipeline artifacts
│   └── processed/           # Final clean datasets
├── logs/                    # Transformation logs
├── models/                  # Saved model artifacts (.pkl / .joblib)
├── evaluation/              # Metrics, plots, backtest results
├── notebooks/               # EDA notebooks
├── src/
│   ├── legacy/              # Old scripts archived here
│   ├── data/
│   │   ├── ingest.py        # Load & validate raw data
│   │   ├── standardize.py   # Column alignment, unified schema
│   │   ├── normalize.py     # Per-90 normalization, baseline adjustment
│   │   └── league_strength.py  # LSC computation
│   ├── features/
│   │   └── engineer.py      # All feature engineering
│   ├── models/
│   │   ├── train.py         # Train XGBoost, LightGBM, MLP, Bayesian
│   │   ├── evaluate.py      # MAE, RMSE, calibration, backtest
│   │   └── adaptation.py    # Adaptation/drop model
│   ├── explainability/
│   │   ├── shap_analysis.py
│   │   └── scenario_sim.py
│   ├── predict.py           # Unified inference endpoint
│   ├── report.py            # Human-readable output report
│   └── pipeline.py          # Orchestrates all phases end-to-end
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md
```

---

### Phase 1 — Data Standardization

#### [NEW] [config.yaml](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/config/config.yaml)
- `raw_data_dir`, `processed_data_dir`, `log_dir`, `model_dir`
- `leagues`: `[Premier League, Bundesliga]`
- `min_minutes`: 600
- `league_strength_coefficients`: `{Premier League: 1.0, Bundesliga: 0.92}`

#### [NEW] [ingest.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/src/data/ingest.py)
- Loads FBRef [players_data-2024_2025.csv](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/players_data-2024_2025.csv)
- Validates required columns exist
- Logs missing players/rows
- Returns typed DataFrame

#### [NEW] [standardize.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/src/data/standardize.py)
- Renames FBRef columns to unified internal schema (`goals_p90`, `xg_p90`, `assists_p90`, `xag_p90`, `npxg_p90`, etc.)
- Filters to configured leagues and min-minutes
- Tags each row with `season` and [league](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/Merger.py#4-46)

#### [NEW] [normalize.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/src/data/normalize.py)
- Computes per-90 for any raw totals not already per-90
- Computes league-average baseline for each stat
- Outputs normalized values relative to league average

#### [NEW] [league_strength.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/src/data/league_strength.py)
- Reads LSC from config
- Computes LSC-adjusted metrics (multiply raw metric by source_LSC / target_LSC)
- Adds `lsc_adjusted_*` columns

---

### Phase 2 — Feature Engineering

#### [NEW] [engineer.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/src/features/engineer.py)
Features created:
- **League-adjusted performance** — raw stat × (source_LSC / target_LSC)
- **Team strength ratio** — player's team xG avg / league xG avg (from FBRef squad data)
- **Possession-adjusted stats** — touches / team possession%
- **Position encoding** — one-hot encode Pos column (GK, DF, MF, FW, and combos)
- **Age curve** — peak performance years 24–28, polynomial decay before/after
- **Play style vector** — progressive passes %, dribble success %, aerial ratio

All transformations logged to `logs/feature_engineering.log`.

Output: `data/processed/feature_dataset.csv`

---

### Phase 3 — Modeling

#### [NEW] [train.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/src/models/train.py)

**Three models trained:**

| Model | Library | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| LightGBM | `lightgbm` | Primary predictor (fast, robust to missing) |
| MLP | `sklearn.neural_network` | Captures nonlinear interactions |
| Bayesian Ridge | `sklearn.linear_model` | Uncertainty quantification |

**Target variables:** `goals_p90`, `assists_p90`, `xg_p90` in the target league.

**Train/test split:** train on Bundesliga 23/24 → predict PL 24/25 for known transfers (backtest). Also do 5-fold CV within each league.

Models saved to `models/lgbm_goals.pkl`, `models/mlp_goals.pkl`, `models/bayesian_goals.pkl`.

#### [NEW] [evaluate.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/src/models/evaluate.py)
- MAE, RMSE per target variable
- Calibration curve (predicted vs actual)
- Transfer backtest: for known Bundesliga→PL transfers, compare prediction to actual
- Results saved to `evaluation/metrics.json` and `evaluation/backtest_report.csv`

---

### Phase 4 — Adaptation Modeling

#### [NEW] [adaptation.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/src/models/adaptation.py)
- Binary classifier: will player be in top 50th percentile within first 10 games?
- Regression: expected number of games to reach baseline performance
- Features: age, position, minutes in source league, league difficulty delta, team strength ratio

---

### Phase 5 — Explainability

#### [NEW] [shap_analysis.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/src/explainability/shap_analysis.py)
- SHAP TreeExplainer for LightGBM models
- Output: top-5 features driving each prediction
- Saved plots to `evaluation/shap_*.png`

#### [NEW] [scenario_sim.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/src/explainability/scenario_sim.py)
- "What-if" simulator: change one feature (e.g. team strength) and re-predict
- Output: sensitivity table

---

### Phase 6 — Inference Endpoint

#### [NEW] [predict.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/src/predict.py)
```
Given: Player name, source_league, target_league, season

Output:
  goals_p90_projected: float
  assists_p90_projected: float
  xg_p90_projected: float
  minutes_expectation: float
  adaptation_score: %
  risk_score: %
  confidence_interval: [low, high]
  top_5_factors: list[str]
```

#### [NEW] [report.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/src/report.py)
- Renders a human-readable text/markdown report for a given player prediction

#### [NEW] [pipeline.py](file:///c:/Shanki/VIT%20CHENNAI/Projs/TransferPred/src/pipeline.py)
- Single entrypoint: `python src/pipeline.py` runs all phases in order
- Accepts `--phase` flag to run individual phases

